  { id: 'counters', level: 'N5', unit: 'Numbers and time', title: `Counting things, people and doses`,
    summary: `The native ひとつ series, counters for people, times, tablets, long and flat things and cups, and where the number goes.`, draft: true,
    body: `<p>Japanese does not put a number directly in front of a noun. It adds a <b>counter</b> that depends on what is being counted, a little like "two sheets of paper" or "three cups of coffee" in English, but for almost everything. In medicine you will use counters for doses, tablets, times per day and people in the family.</p>
<h3>The native series: ひとつ to とお</h3>
<p>For things that have no special counter, and for answering "how many", Japanese uses an old native set of numbers that goes up to ten. The question word is いくつ.</p>
<table><tr><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th><th>5</th></tr>
<tr><td>一《ひと》つ</td><td>二《ふた》つ</td><td>三《みっ》つ</td><td>四《よっ》つ</td><td>五《いつ》つ</td></tr>
<tr><th>6</th><th>7</th><th>8</th><th>9</th><th>10</th></tr>
<tr><td>六《むっ》つ</td><td>七《なな》つ</td><td>八《やっ》つ</td><td>九《ここの》つ</td><td>十《とお》</td></tr></table>
<h3>Common counters</h3>
<table><tr><th>Counter</th><th>For</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>6</th><th>How many?</th></tr>
<tr><td>人《にん》</td><td>people</td><td>一人《ひとり》</td><td>二人《ふたり》</td><td>三人《さんにん》</td><td>六人《ろくにん》</td><td>何人《なんにん》</td></tr>
<tr><td>回《かい》</td><td>times</td><td>一回《いっかい》</td><td>二回《にかい》</td><td>三回《さんかい》</td><td>六回《ろっかい》</td><td>何回《なんかい》</td></tr>
<tr><td>錠《じょう》</td><td>tablets</td><td>一錠《いちじょう》</td><td>二錠《にじょう》</td><td>三錠《さんじょう》</td><td>六錠《ろくじょう》</td><td>何錠《なんじょう》</td></tr>
<tr><td>本《ほん》</td><td>long things: bottles, cigarettes</td><td>一本《いっぽん》</td><td>二本《にほん》</td><td>三本《さんぼん》</td><td>六本《ろっぽん》</td><td>何本《なんぼん》</td></tr>
<tr><td>枚《まい》</td><td>flat things: paper, sheets</td><td>一枚《いちまい》</td><td>二枚《にまい》</td><td>三枚《さんまい》</td><td>六枚《ろくまい》</td><td>何枚《なんまい》</td></tr>
<tr><td>杯《はい》</td><td>cups, glasses</td><td>一杯《いっぱい》</td><td>二杯《にはい》</td><td>三杯《さんばい》</td><td>六杯《ろっぱい》</td><td>何杯《なんばい》</td></tr>
<tr><td>歳《さい》</td><td>years of age</td><td>一歳《いっさい》</td><td>二歳《にさい》</td><td>三歳《さんさい》</td><td>六歳《ろくさい》</td><td>何歳《なんさい》</td></tr></table>
<p>People are irregular only for one and two. Four people is 四人《よにん》. Other useful forms: 八回《はっかい》, 十回《じゅっかい》, 八本《はっぽん》, 十本《じゅっぽん》.</p>
<h3>Where the number goes</h3>
<p>The usual order is: noun + particle, then number + counter, then the verb. The number with its counter needs no particle of its own. To say "per", use に: 一日《いちにち》 に 二回《にかい》 (twice a day), 週《しゅう》 に 三回《さんかい》 (three times a week).</p>
<div class="ex"><b>りんご を 一《ひと》つ ください。</b><span>One apple, please.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>家族《かぞく》 は 何人《なんにん》 です か。</b><span>How many people are in your family?</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>四人《よにん》 です。</b><span>Four.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>子《こ》ども が 二人《ふたり》 います。</b><span>I have two children.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>一人《ひとり》 で 住《す》んで います。</b><span>I live alone.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>薬《くすり》 を 一日《いちにち》 に 二回《にかい》 飲《の》みます。</b><span>I take the medicine twice a day.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>一回《いっかい》 に 一錠《いちじょう》 飲《の》んで ください。</b><span>Please take one tablet each time.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>寝《ね》る 前《まえ》 に 二錠《にじょう》 です。</b><span>Two tablets before bed.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>週《しゅう》 に 何回《なんかい》 お酒《さけ》 を 飲《の》みます か。</b><span>How many times a week do you drink alcohol?</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>週《しゅう》 に 三回《さんかい》 ぐらい です。</b><span>About three times a week.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>たばこ を 一日《いちにち》 に 何本《なんぼん》 吸《す》います か。</b><span>How many cigarettes do you smoke a day?</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>十本《じゅっぽん》 ぐらい です。</b><span>About ten.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>コーヒー を 一日《いちにち》 に 三杯《さんばい》 飲《の》みます。</b><span>I drink three cups of coffee a day.</span></div>
<div class="ex"><b>紙《かみ》 を 一枚《いちまい》 ください。</b><span>A sheet of paper, please.</span></div>
<div class="note"><b>Common mistake:</b> putting the number in front of the noun as in English. Say 薬《くすり》 を 二錠《にじょう》 飲《の》みます (take two tablets of the medicine), with the number after the particle, not 二錠《にじょう》 薬《くすり》.</div>`,
    quiz: [
      [`How do you say "two people"?`, [`ににん`, `ふたり`, `ふたにん`], 1, `二人《ふたり》 is irregular.`],
      [`How do you say "four people"?`, [`よんにん`, `しにん`, `よにん`], 2, `四人《よにん》 uses the reading よ.`],
      [`How do you say "six times"?`, [`ろっかい`, `ろくかい`, `むかい`], 0, `六回《ろっかい》 has a small っ.`],
      [`Which counter is used for tablets?`, [`枚《まい》`, `錠《じょう》`, `杯《はい》`], 1, `錠《じょう》 counts tablets; 枚《まい》 counts flat things and 杯《はい》 counts cups.`],
      [`Which sentence correctly says "I take the medicine twice a day"?`, [`二回《にかい》 薬《くすり》 一日《いちにち》 を 飲《の》みます。`, `一日《いちにち》 の 薬《くすり》 二回《にかい》 に 飲《の》みます。`, `薬《くすり》 を 一日《いちにち》 に 二回《にかい》 飲《の》みます。`], 2, `Noun + particle, then 一日《いちにち》 に 二回《にかい》, then the verb.`],
      [`How do you say "three cigarettes"?`, [`さんほん`, `さんぼん`, `さんぽん`], 1, `三本《さんぼん》 changes ほん to ぼん.`]
    ] }
